      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the test. The main understandability issues are:\n1. Five constants (`TEXT_LATIN1`, etc.) and two methods (`checkXmlWriter`, `createXmlContent`) are defined but never used by `testNoXmlHeader`\n2. The `checkXmlContent` helper is cryptic — `writerCheck` is kept just to call `getEncoding()` after close, and the intent of each assertion is unclear\n3. Variable names like `writerCheck` don't convey purpose\n\nI'll produce a cleaned-up version that removes the dead code, clarifies variable names, and adds brief comments explaining the intent of each assertion.The compile script expects the file in the `testNoXmlHeader` directory. I wrote it to `testNoXmlHead` (typo in my path). Let me write it to the correct location.The improved test compiled successfully. The key understandability changes made:\n\n- **Removed dead code**: Five unused constants (`TEXT_LATIN1`, `TEXT_LATIN7`, `TEXT_LATIN15`, `TEXT_EUC_JP`, `TEXT_UNICODE`) and two unused methods (`checkXmlWriter`, `createXmlContent`) were dropped — they belonged to broader test suites but had no role in `testNoXmlHeader`.\n- **Renamed variables for clarity**: `out` → `capturedOutput`, `writerCheck` → `closedWriter`, `charset`/`writerCharset` → `expectedCharset`/`resolvedCharset` — names now convey purpose.\n- **Extracted the XML string into a named variable** in `testNoXmlHeader` so the intent is self-documenting.\n- **Added Javadoc and inline comments** explaining the fallback-to-UTF-8 contract being tested and the reason each assertion exists (including the non-obvious `contains()` check for charset aliases and the `@SuppressWarnings` justification).\n- **Removed the unused `@DefaultLocale` import** from the original."
    }
